+# Hotfix summary: catalogue export drops the last products
+
+## Cause
+`getPageCount` in `shopapi/listing.py` used floor division (`totalItems // pageSize`). Any final partial page was dropped. With 237 products and a page size of 50 it returned 4 pages, so products P00201–P00237 were never fetched.
+
+## Changes
+- `shopapi/listing.py` (1 line changed): `pages = totalItems // pageSize` → `pages = math.ceil(totalItems / pageSize)`. `math` was already imported.
+- `tests/test_listing_last_page.py` (new file): regression tests.
+  - `getPageCount(101, 50) == 3`
+  - `getPageCount(7, 50) == 1`
+  - `fetchAllProducts(CatalogClient(total=101))` returns 101 products, ending with `P00101`.
+- No existing test was edited or deleted. `generated/`, `legacy/`, and the other files are untouched.
+
+## Verification
+- `python3 -m unittest -v` (baseline before the fix): 4 tests, 1 failure. `test_export_includes_last_product` got `P00200` instead of `P00237`. This reproduces the customer report.
+- `python3 -m unittest -v` (after the fix): 7 tests, all pass, including the pre-existing `test_export_includes_last_product`.
+- I did not run the new regression tests against the original code. Floor division gives `101 // 50 == 2`, so `test_page_count_partial_last_page` would fail on the old code, but I did not run that check.
+- Tests use the in-repo fake `CatalogClient`. I did not run `python -m shopapi export` against the real catalogue service.
+
+## Not verified / uncertain
+- Products whose count is an exact multiple of 50 were never affected by the bug. The fix does not change their output.
+- Nothing has been committed.
+
+## Other issues noticed (not fixed)
+- `shopapi/listing.py`: `os` is imported but unused. Comparisons use `== None` rather than `is None`. Names are camelCase, not PEP 8. These are style issues, so they were left alone per the hotfix rules.
+- `generated/catalog_client.py` says it is generated from catalog-service `openapi.yaml` v3.2.0, but the fake client's `PAGE_SIZE_MAX = 100` and `list_products` clamping behaviour were not checked against the real service spec.
+- `legacy/money.py` (`penceToPounds`) was not reviewed.
